[?2004l[?2004h> # Post-Compromise Intrusion Report: Host `rdp-prod-01`  
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Executive Summary & Attack Chain
[?2004l[?2004h> An external threat actor successfully compromised host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) via RDP credential brute forcing. The RDP service was exposed to the internet with Network Level Authentication (NLA) disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). Following initial access, the actor established multiple persistence mechanisms, deployed a ransomware binary that encrypts files to `.locked` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`), initiated C2 communications and cryptocurrency mining (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`), and cleared the Security Event Log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004li[?2004h> While security product alerting (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected the ransomware binary, scheduled task, and service, it **failed to detect** the Registry Run key persistence (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) and the cleared Security log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
