[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 5. Security Telemetry & Gap Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The SAS alert feed (`/sas/alerts.json`) covered three threat items:
[?2004l[?2004h> - `ALERT-01`: Ransomware binary (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - `ALERT-02`: Scheduled task (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - `ALERT-03`: Malicious service (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - `ALERT-04`: RDP baseline weakness (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Coverage Gaps Identified**:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Registry Run Key Persistence**: Present in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` but missing from security alerts.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Event Log Cleared Anti-Forensics**: Present in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx` (Event ID 1102) but missing from security alerts.
