==> /app/intrusion-report.md <==
# Post-Compromise Intrusion Report: Host `rdp-prod-01`  

## 1. Executive Summary & Attack Chain
An external threat actor successfully compromised host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) via RDP credential brute forcing. The RDP service was exposed to the internet with Network Level Authentication (NLA) disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). Following initial access, the actor established multiple persistence mechanisms, deployed a ransomware binary that encrypts files to `.locked` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`), initiated C2 communications and cryptocurrency mining (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`), and cleared the Security Event Log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).

While security product alerting (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected the ransomware binary, scheduled task, and service, it **failed to detect** the Registry Run key persistence (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) and the cleared Security log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).

---

## 2. MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping

| ATT&CK ID | Technique Name | Tactic | Evidence / Finding | Alert Status | Citation |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **T1110** | Brute Force | Credential Access | External RDP brute force attack | Alerted | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11` |
| **T1021.001** | Remote Desktop Protocol | Lateral Movement | RDP logon allowed without NLA | Alerted | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4` |
| **T1059.001** | PowerShell | Execution | Execution of PowerShell post-compromise scripts | Alerted | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` |
| **T1486** | Data Encrypted for Impact | Impact | Ransomware `svc.exe` encrypts user files to `.locked` | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |
| **T1053.005** | Scheduled Task | Execution / Persistence | Scheduled task `UpdateHelper` runs `svc.exe` every 5 min | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` |
| **T1547.001** | Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder | Persistence | Run key `svc -> C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` | **SILENT** | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |
| **T1543.003** | Windows Service | Persistence | Service `svc-helper` / `svc-helper.sys` installed | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` |

